"answer": "Project Zenith is an initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics and optimizing cloud storage solutions for enhanced security and accessibility. The project was initially introduced with a kickoff scheduled for mid-2023 (dates vary between June 15th and July 15th in different communications) and a phase one budget of $500,000. Leadership has included Sarah Tan, Marcus Cole, and later Omar Jensen as lead developer. The team has expanded multiple times, adding members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, with onboarding sessions held in September. Key phases include design, development, and testing, with a significant milestone reached in October marking the completion of the testing phase. The project focuses on leveraging AI for data visualization tools, with a call for ideas submitted by July 20th. Additionally, the compliance plan budget was increased to $55,000 for training and audits, and feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience was sought by the end of November."
